    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's just... the sheer exhaustion of it all. People always talk about \"fighting\" or \"resilience,\" but that assumes there's some noble reward at the end of the struggle. When you look at it objectively, isn't there a quiet dignity in recognizing when a cycle has reached its natural conclusion? Like deciding to step out of a room that has become too loud and too empty all at once.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
